Let the MIGraphX execution provider take GridSample

MIGraphX parses and runs ONNX GridSample (bilinear, zeros, align_corners), but the
provider's op list omits it, so every GridSample stays on the CPU and splits the graph
into partitions around it. On a DEIM/D-FINE detector that leaves a partition of one Slice
and one Reshape whose output MIGraphX returns as a strided view (BACKLOG CON225). With
GridSample on the list the model is one partition. Not in v1.31.0 or v1.31.1 (checked
2026-11-04).

--- a/onnxruntime/core/providers/migraphx/migraphx_execution_provider.cc
+++ b/onnxruntime/core/providers/migraphx/migraphx_execution_provider.cc
@@ -916,6 +916,7 @@
                                                     "GlobalMaxPool",
                                                     "Greater",
                                                     "GreaterOrEqual",
+                                                    "GridSample",
                                                     "GroupNormalization",
                                                     "GroupNorm",
                                                     "GroupQueryAttention",
